WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.640
Endometriosis is
a condition where

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.480
tissue, similar to the
lining in your uterus,

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.520
grows in other
areas of your body.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.140
If you are a woman,
your reproductive system

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:32.690
includes the vagina, uterus,
fallopian tubes, and ovaries.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:34.910
During a normal
menstrual cycle, you're

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:40.040
ovaries make chemicals
called hormones, which

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.570
signal the lining of
your uterus to thicken.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.380
The lining, called
the endometrium,

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.760
builds up to prepare to
receive a fertilized egg.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.010
If the egg isn't
fertilized, the uterus

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:58.160
sheds the lining
through your vagina.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.055
This monthly bleeding is
called your menstrual period.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.040
If you have endometriosis,
the lining type tissue

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.570
grows outside your uterus for
reasons that aren't clear.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.650
The misplaced tissue
response to the hormones

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:19.790
just like it would if it
were inside your uterus.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.000
The tissue continues
to thicken, then

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.280
sheds, and bleeds with
every menstrual cycle.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.980
However, the blood
and tissue that

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.560
are shed outside the uterus
have no way to leave your body.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.430
The trapped endometrial flow can
irritate the surrounding area

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.225
causing inflammation and pain.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.710
Bands of scar tissue,
called adhesions,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.020
may form, sticking
one organ to another

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.270
or causing your
fallopian tubes to close.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.340
This can affect your
fertility, which

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.370
is the ability to
become pregnant.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:02.570
Endometriosis can form
endometriomas, also known

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.340
as chocolate cysts.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.670
These cysts are fluid
filled sacs on your ovaries

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:08.865
that can affect fertility.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:15.545
Endometriosis may also
result in abnormal bleeding.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.180
The most common sites
for endometriosis

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:26.090
are the ovaries,
fallopian tubes,

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:29.840
the outside of your uterus,
the supporting structures

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.420
around your uterus, and
the lining of your pelvis,

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.510
called the peritoneum.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:41.380
Other sites include
your bladder, rectum,

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:44.000
and intestines.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:48.250
If you have endometriosis,
you may have one or more

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.800
of these symptoms,
chronic usually worsening

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:57.930
central pelvic pain, pain before
or during your period, pain

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.730
during sex felt deep
within your pelvis,

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:05.050
painful urination
during your period,

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.300
painful bowel movements
during your period,

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:13.680
abnormal bleeding, diarrhea,
constipation, or nausea,

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.373
and difficulty getting
pregnant called infertility.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.050
Your doctor may recommend
treatment options

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:28.730
from the following categories,
pain management medications,

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.050
such as aspirin,
acetaminophen, or non-steroidal

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.400
anti-inflammatory drugs,
also known as nsaids,

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.230
provide relief from pain.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.120
Hormone therapy, such
as birth control pills,

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.160
can prevent monthly endometrial
buildup and bleeding.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.690
You may need a
surgical procedure

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:52.970
to treat the tissue
causing pain or bleeding.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:57.150
Examples of such procedures
include, removal or destruction

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:06.200
of endometrial issue, removal
of adhesions and scar tissue,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:13.300
removal or drainage of
cysts, removal or destruction

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:21.570
of nerve fibers that transmit
pain, removal of your uterus,

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:27.280
called a hysterectomy, or
removal of your ovaries,

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.490
called an oophorectomy.

